## Report

**File written (only one):** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` — untracked/new in this phase, `git status` shows `??`. The two modified siblings (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`) are pre-existing sibling-worker writes; I made no write call to either. Code sits outside the `BEGIN/END GENERATED MODE COMMANDS` markers, which are still intact (count 2).

**What changed**
- `export const DEPTH_WORDING: readonly string[]` — 15 phrases: `in depth`, `deep dive`, `deep research`, `deep review`, `thorough`, `thoroughly`, `exhaustive`, `iteratively`, `multiple passes`, `many passes`, `several passes`, `council`, `several models`, `final verdict`, `everything you can`. No bare topic words. `thorough`/`thoroughly` are separate entries because whole-word matching does not stem.
- `escapePhrase()` + module-level `DEPTH_REQUEST = new RegExp('\\b(?:…)\\b')` — one alternation, one test per prompt, whole-word on both ends so `thorough` cannot fire inside a longer word.
- `_prompt` renamed to `prompt`; the `system-deep-loop` gate sits after the own-key table lookup and returns `undefined` unless the prompt contains `/deep:` (lowercased) or matches `DEPTH_REQUEST`. Every other hub is untouched.

